00:15:46.697 --> 00:15:49.032
This is the area code

00:15:46.697 --> 00:15:49.032
for Juarez, Mexico.

00:15:49.032 --> 00:15:50.492
He's trying to get

00:15:49.032 --> 00:15:50.492
over the border!

00:15:50.534 --> 00:15:52.410
You think so?

00:15:50.534 --> 00:15:52.410
Definitely.

00:15:52.452 --> 00:15:54.204
There's only one road

00:15:52.452 --> 00:15:54.204
into Juarez,

00:15:54.245 --> 00:15:55.622
and it goes

00:15:54.245 --> 00:15:55.622
through El Paso.

00:15:55.664 --> 00:15:57.040
We got to get

00:15:55.664 --> 00:15:57.040
to El Paso.

00:15:57.081 --> 00:15:58.625
Joe, how do you know

00:15:58.667 --> 00:16:00.210
the area code for

00:15:58.667 --> 00:16:00.210
Juarez, Mexico?

00:16:00.251 --> 00:16:03.171
There was a stem cell doctor

00:16:00.251 --> 00:16:03.171
I went down there to see.

00:16:03.213 --> 00:16:06.216
He just rubbed, like,

00:16:03.213 --> 00:16:06.216
salsa on my legs.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:11.221
Hey, you're not

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:11.221
in uniform.

00:16:11.262 --> 00:16:13.139
Are you guys cops?

00:16:13.181 --> 00:16:14.725
Are you guys cops?

00:16:14.766 --> 00:16:16.267
They know we're not cops!

00:16:16.309 --> 00:16:17.310
(tires squealing)

00:16:22.858 --> 00:16:24.234
All right, guys,

00:16:22.858 --> 00:16:24.234
the next flight

00:16:24.275 --> 00:16:25.694
to El Paso leaves

00:16:24.275 --> 00:16:25.694
in 40 minutes.

00:16:25.736 --> 00:16:27.111
But Briggs is ahead of us.

00:16:27.153 --> 00:16:28.321
Won't he already be there?

00:16:28.363 --> 00:16:30.198
No, he'd never risk

00:16:28.363 --> 00:16:30.198
going through an airport.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:31.742
Too many cops,

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:31.742
too many cameras,

00:16:31.783 --> 00:16:32.826
too much security.

00:16:32.868 --> 00:16:34.118
I don't know, Joe.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:35.704
Sometimes the

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:35.704
security's pretty lax.

00:16:35.746 --> 00:16:38.081
I mean, the last plane

00:16:35.746 --> 00:16:38.081
I was on got gay-jacked.

00:16:38.081 --> 00:16:40.625
This plane's going to Miami!

00:16:40.667 --> 00:16:42.252
(passengers gasp)

00:16:42.293 --> 00:16:44.087
(electronic dance music playing)

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:53.638
Hey, Lois?

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.139
Shh. Quiet, Brian.

00:16:55.181 --> 00:16:57.100
Mom's taking a nap

00:16:55.181 --> 00:16:57.100
on the couch.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.852
Yeah. And look,

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.852
she fell asleep

00:16:58.894 --> 00:17:01.229
with the cat right

00:16:58.894 --> 00:17:01.229
on her chest.

00:17:03.147 --> 00:17:04.482
(purring)

00:17:09.404 --> 00:17:11.322
Isn't that cute?

00:17:12.908 --> 00:17:14.910
(purring)

00:17:24.252 --> 00:17:25.295
Meow.

00:17:25.336 --> 00:17:27.338
Purr. Purr.

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.340
I think you're dreaming.

00:17:29.382 --> 00:17:31.635
No, I'm not.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:39.142
BRIAN:

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:39.142
Stupid cat!

00:17:42.771 --> 00:17:44.272
God, it's so damn hot.

00:17:44.314 --> 00:17:45.690
Hey, I got an idea.

00:17:45.732 --> 00:17:48.318
Let's make

00:17:45.732 --> 00:17:48.318
scalding asphalt angels.

00:17:48.359 --> 00:17:50.403
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:17:50.445 --> 00:17:51.780
(sizzling)

00:17:51.822 --> 00:17:54.741
Second-degree burns;

00:17:51.822 --> 00:17:54.741
first-degree fun.

00:17:54.783 --> 00:17:57.160
Geez, how long we got to

00:17:54.783 --> 00:17:57.160
stand out here like this?

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.328
Till Briggs comes through.

00:17:58.369 --> 00:17:59.830
You know, I was thinking

00:17:58.369 --> 00:17:59.830
about that, Joe.

00:17:59.871 --> 00:18:02.373
If Briggs is driving here,

00:17:59.871 --> 00:18:02.373
that's like 2,000 miles.

00:18:02.415 --> 00:18:04.208
It's going to be at

00:18:02.415 --> 00:18:04.208
least a couple of days.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:06.210
Huh. I guess you're right.

00:18:06.252 --> 00:18:08.755
Well, what are we going to do

00:18:06.252 --> 00:18:08.755
for two days in El Paso?

00:18:10.256 --> 00:18:12.175
There's a Chicano

00:18:10.256 --> 00:18:12.175
heritage festival.

00:18:12.175 --> 00:18:13.301
No way.

00:18:13.343 --> 00:18:14.970
KC and the Sunshine Band

00:18:13.343 --> 00:18:14.970
is playing.

00:18:15.012 --> 00:18:16.220
Why?

00:18:16.262 --> 00:18:17.388
Or we could visit

00:18:16.262 --> 00:18:17.388
the Pershing House

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:19.223
where John Pershing

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:19.223
took control

00:18:19.265 --> 00:18:21.476
of the Eighth Army

00:18:19.265 --> 00:18:21.476
Brigade in 1914.

00:18:22.769 --> 00:18:24.187
So, that's his bed?

00:18:22.769 --> 00:18:24.187
Yes.

00:18:24.228 --> 00:18:25.313
So, that's his desk?

00:18:24.228 --> 00:18:25.313
Yes.

00:18:25.355 --> 00:18:26.940
So, that's his lamp?

00:18:25.355 --> 00:18:26.940
Yes.

00:18:26.982 --> 00:18:28.316
So, that's his dresser?

00:18:26.982 --> 00:18:28.316
Yes.

00:18:28.358 --> 00:18:29.776
So, that's his window?

00:18:28.358 --> 00:18:29.776
Yes.

00:18:29.818 --> 00:18:31.277
So, that's his floor?

00:18:29.818 --> 00:18:31.277
Yes.

00:18:31.319 --> 00:18:32.863
Wow.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:38.409
What do you got

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:38.409
there, Quagmire?

00:18:38.451 --> 00:18:39.536
Is that Briggs?

00:18:39.577 --> 00:18:40.871
No, this guy's clean.

00:18:40.912 --> 00:18:42.539
Well, send him through.

00:18:40.912 --> 00:18:42.539
What's the holdup?

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:44.207
Sombreros! Maracas!

00:18:44.207 --> 00:18:46.084
Ceramic Winnie the Pooh dolls!

00:18:46.209 --> 00:18:47.293
Get 'em now, folks!

00:18:47.335 --> 00:18:49.295
You're not going to find

00:18:47.335 --> 00:18:49.295
this stuff in Mexico!

00:18:50.421 --> 00:18:52.841
Come on. What's

00:18:50.421 --> 00:18:52.841
going on up there?

00:18:52.883 --> 00:18:54.634
Briggs.

00:18:58.221 --> 00:19:00.223
Damn it!

00:18:58.221 --> 00:19:00.223
He's getting away!

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:24.247
(grunts)

00:19:27.125 --> 00:19:29.794
You're not going to get away

00:19:27.125 --> 00:19:29.794
this time, you son of a bitch.

00:19:29.836 --> 00:19:31.295
Please, don't kill me.

00:19:31.337 --> 00:19:32.422
I'm not married.

00:19:32.463 --> 00:19:33.798
My life is awesome.

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:36.843
I've waited 15 years

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:36.843
for this moment, Briggs.

00:19:36.885 --> 00:19:38.845
Do you have any idea

00:19:36.885 --> 00:19:38.845
what it's like

00:19:38.887 --> 00:19:41.723
to have to lift yourself

00:19:38.887 --> 00:19:41.723
into a wheelchair every morning?

00:19:41.765 --> 00:19:44.475
To have your wife look at you

00:19:41.765 --> 00:19:44.475
like you're half a man?

00:19:44.517 --> 00:19:46.269
To get preferential parking?

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:48.271
To board a plane early

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:48.271
with the first-class people

00:19:48.312 --> 00:19:49.731
and gold card members?

00:19:49.773 --> 00:19:51.315
All right, it's not all bad.

00:19:51.357 --> 00:19:53.443
But I'm not going to kill you.

00:19:53.484 --> 00:19:55.904
I'm not an animal like you.

00:19:55.946 --> 00:19:57.614
So, what are you going to do,

00:19:55.946 --> 00:19:57.614
arrest me?

00:19:57.655 --> 00:19:58.823
No.

00:19:58.865 --> 00:20:00.700
I don't arrest cripples.

00:20:00.742 --> 00:20:03.453
(groaning)

00:20:03.494 --> 00:20:05.288
By the way, you're under arrest.

00:20:05.329 --> 00:20:07.540
I only said that last thing

00:20:05.329 --> 00:20:07.540
'cause it seemed cool.

00:20:07.582 --> 00:20:09.500
Oh, my God,

00:20:07.582 --> 00:20:09.500
that was so awesome.

00:20:09.542 --> 00:20:10.668
I saw everything.

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:12.295
You were all like...

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:12.295
(deep mumbling)

00:20:12.336 --> 00:20:13.880
And Briggs was all like...

00:20:12.336 --> 00:20:13.880
(high-pitched mumbling)

00:20:13.922 --> 00:20:15.673
And then you were all like...

00:20:13.922 --> 00:20:15.673
(mimics two gunshots)

00:20:15.715 --> 00:20:17.425
And then Briggs's legs

00:20:15.715 --> 00:20:17.425
were like...

00:20:17.467 --> 00:20:19.094
(mimics video game

00:20:17.467 --> 00:20:19.094
sound effects)

00:20:19.136 --> 00:20:20.470
Oh, crap, he's dead.

00:20:20.511 --> 00:20:21.721
I think he bled out.

00:20:21.763 --> 00:20:23.431
I must have hit

00:20:21.763 --> 00:20:23.431
the femoral artery.

00:20:23.473 --> 00:20:25.809
Ah, just kick him into Mexico.

00:20:30.188 --> 00:20:32.440
Guys, I can't thank you

00:20:30.188 --> 00:20:32.440
enough for what you did.

00:20:32.482 --> 00:20:34.484
You risked your

00:20:32.482 --> 00:20:34.484
lives for me,

00:20:34.525 --> 00:20:35.986
and I couldn't have

00:20:34.525 --> 00:20:35.986
done it without you.

00:20:36.027 --> 00:20:37.487
Hey, that's what

00:20:36.027 --> 00:20:37.487
pals are for.

00:20:37.528 --> 00:20:38.905
Yeah, and thanks for letting me

00:20:38.947 --> 00:20:40.490
fire a few rounds

00:20:38.947 --> 00:20:40.490
into Briggs's corpse.

00:20:40.531 --> 00:20:43.493
That was the most powerful

00:20:40.531 --> 00:20:43.493
I've felt in a couple years.

00:20:43.534 --> 00:20:44.744
Well, you guys helped me

00:20:44.786 --> 00:20:46.370
finally have some closure

00:20:44.786 --> 00:20:46.370
in my life.

00:20:46.412 --> 00:20:49.540
I feel like a new man--

00:20:46.412 --> 00:20:49.540
like I'm reborn.

00:20:49.582 --> 00:20:52.169
Joe, you have blood just

00:20:49.582 --> 00:20:52.169
pouring out of your pant leg.

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:55.213
Yeah, I had a ball

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:55.213
blow in the river.